                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">couple of different ways that you can get started to create a web app in Azure. Azure offers a couple
of different services. So, you can use Azure Web Apps, container-based web apps. I can do it through
DevOps or I can even create a serverless web app through Azure. Functions.




To learn the differences between these, you can click on the card where you can learn more and
understand what is this in the first place? Why would I want to use it? How does this web app
connect to other services in Azure through this reference architecture diagram? What are some of
the prerequisites that I might need and see about pricing? And you can see here that you can create
ten web apps for free with my Azure free account.




Here, click on create. You will be landed on the create a form for the web app and you just need to fill
out a few key details before you can create my web app resource. So, you just need to fill out the
subscription, resource group, or you can create a new one, the name of your web app, pick your
runtime stack and operating system as well as region. And, just click review and create.
If you want to get back to the Azure home, just click on the top. It returns you to home.




And you can see because you have recently accessed Quickstart Center, it’s going to show up in my
Azure services. So, whenever you click on a resource in Azure Service in Azure it’s going to show up in
your recent Azure services, which makes it really easy to find and come back to, so you can go on and
create your second project in Azure.
Microsoft Azure - Getting Free Trial with Azure Quickstart Center</pre>
